data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"content":"\n\nSources:\n- As the US and China form AI blocs, countries are increasingly torn between them: https://apnews.com/article/9974a3e5dc955a93935d131a4aeb8886?utm_source=openai\n- To make AI morally good, tech companies are turning to religion. But some say it isn't that simple: https://apnews.com/article/2bb91e3334fd6d732edf22288cabf4ec?utm_source=openai\n- New UN initiative will aim to tackle the military uses of AI: https://apnews.com/article/e0a3c48c91a9de89cab72609d185f658?utm_source=openai\n- A Chinese hacker used AI agents to break into more than 100 company websites: https://www.tomshardware.com/tech-industry/artificial-intelligence/a-chinese-hacker-used-ai-agents-to-break-into-more-than-100-company-websites-deere-and-sharkninja-among-websites-hit-by-open-source-ai-powered-problem-solving-platform-demo?utm_source=openai\n- Sharp drops for AI stocks overwhelm markets worldwide as oil prices jump: https://apnews.com/article/33767691a4a0730b96d6f0c5100ea9b2?utm_source=openai\n- AI agents are only as good as the personal information you share. That raises privacy concerns: https://apnews.com/article/449734d41d3750aad7038b761faa49c9?utm_source=openai"},"finish_reason":null,"index":0}],"created":1792949858,"id":"resp_07ceb9118c919c37016ade3e62bb8c87d0b1997019a7121286","model":"gpt-5.6-luna","object":"chat.completion.chunk"}

